{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Carried from the Gerrit `LLM-Review` bot on change 3211 patchset 2 (advisory, non-blocking), because this ticket consumes the number the finding is about.\n\n`tests/integration/test_similar_tickets_scale.py:240`, in `test_the_cold_catch_up_cost_at_that_scale_is_emitted_as_a_number`, ends with:\n\n```python\nassert isinstance(p95, float)\nassert p95 > 0.0\n```\n\nAny wall-clock sample satisfies both unconditionally. The test cannot fail for any behavior of the code under test, so it is a measurement emitter wearing a test's name, not a regression oracle.\n\nThat matters here because this ticket records \"the measured cold-catch-up p95\" in ADR 0122. The number that test prints is the number this ADR will cite, and nothing currently checks it against anything.\n\nTwo separable things to settle when this ticket is worked:\n\n1. Which p95 the ADR cites, and on what hardware. A wall-clock figure measured on one host is not portable; 47c8 already had to replace a wall-clock budget with a counted invariant plus a same-host ratio after `macos-latest` measured 545 ms against a 500 ms budget where the same code measured 107 ms locally. The ADR should say what was measured, on what, rather than present a bare millisecond figure as a property of the code.\n2. Whether that test keeps a name that claims it tests something. Either it gains an assertion that can fail, or it is renamed and documented as a measurement harness.\n\nNo change was made to the test under 47c8: the finding is advisory and 47c8 is the keystone blocking this ticket, 80a5 and 2041, so resetting its gates for a non-blocking test-naming issue was not worth the round trip."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793594124407534717,"uuid":"51630d92-2a8e-4ff1-880a-a3e853c5cb6e"}